VERDICT: the smallest 1st-percentile L1C digital number across all baselines and sampled bands is 15.
  => it is < 1000, so a +1000 add-offset would force negative TOA reflectance (impossible). The stored data is on the plain 0-10000 no-offset scale; reflectance = DN * 1e-4 is correct, and is consistent across all eight baselines. Product-aware re-normalization (z-scoring by each product's own per-band mean/std) is additionally invariant to any constant per-band offset.

